# ROWNAA — Phase 4: Admin Panel (All 9 Panels)

> The admin is the platform controller. Every piece of data flows through here. This panel must be designed for efficiency — minimal clicks to approve, manage, and monitor. On mobile it must feel like a management app.

---

## Admin Panel Layout (Desktop)

### Sidebar (Fixed Left, 240px wide)
- Top: Rownaa logo + "Admin Panel" label
- Navigation items (with icons):
  1. Dashboard (home icon)
  2. Registrations (user-check icon)
  3. Bookings (calendar icon)
  4. Payments (credit-card icon)
  5. Subscriptions (star icon)
  6. Content (layout icon)
  7. Customers (users icon)
  8. Notifications (bell icon)
  9. Settings / Roles (shield icon)
- Bottom: Admin avatar + name + "Logout" link
- Active item: left border accent color + background tint

### Main Content Area
- Top bar: Page title (left) + Notification bell with badge count (right) + Admin avatar
- Content below top bar, full width, scrollable

---

## Admin Panel Layout (Mobile) — App-Like

- NO sidebar on mobile
- Top bar: "ROWNAA Admin" text (left) + Notification bell (right)
- Bottom navigation bar (fixed, 5 icons): Dashboard | Registrations | Bookings | Payments | More (opens a sheet with remaining items)
- All data tables converted to swipeable cards on mobile
- Filter/search → opens as a bottom sheet slide-up panel

---

## Panel 1 — Dashboard (Overview)

### KPI Row (4 cards)
| Card | Data Source | Period Selector |
|---|---|---|
| Total Bookings | COUNT bookings | Today / This Week / This Month toggle |
| Total Revenue | SUM final_amount | Same toggle |
| Commission Earned | SUM commission_amount | Same toggle |
| Pending Actions | COUNT pending bookings + pending registrations | Always live |

### Charts Row
- Chart 1: Line chart — Bookings over last 30 days
- Chart 2: Donut chart — Booking status distribution (Pending / Confirmed / Ongoing / Completed / Cancelled)
- Chart 3: Bar chart — Revenue by service type

### Alerts Section
- Red alert cards for: Fitness certs expiring in ≤7 days (list of car plate + expiry date + owner name + "View Car" link)
- Orange alert cards for: Tax tokens expiring in ≤7 days (same format)
- Yellow alert cards for: Subscriptions expiring in ≤7 days

### Quick Actions Row
- "New Registration Requests" → count badge + "Review" button → navigates to Panel 2
- "Pending Bookings" → count + "Assign" button → navigates to Panel 3
- "Today's Trips" → count + "View" button

---

## Panel 2 — Owner Registration Panel

### 2A — Registration Queue Page

**Filters Bar:**
- Status filter tabs: All | Pending | Approved | Rejected (tab bar style)
- Dropdown filter: Business Type (Individual / Agency)
- Dropdown filter: Area / Zone
- Date range filter: Submitted between [date] and [date]
- Search box: "Search by owner name or phone"

**Table Columns (Desktop):**
| # | Owner/Business Name | Phone | Type | Area | Submitted | Status | Action |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

**Card Format (Mobile):**
- Owner name (bold) + phone
- Type badge + Area tag
- Submitted date + Status badge
- "Review" button (accent, full-width)

**Clicking "Review" on any row → opens 2B (Business Review)**

---

### 2B — Business/Company Level Review Page

**Header:** Owner/Business Name | Submission date | Status badge

**Section 1 — Basic Info (read-only display)**
- Name, Phone (✓ OTP Verified badge), Email, Business Type, Area/Operating Zone

**Section 2 — Identity Documents**
- NID Front: [Image viewer — click to enlarge in lightbox]
- NID Back: [Image viewer]
- Trade License: [Image viewer or "Not Applicable"]
- Address Proof: [Image viewer]

**Section 3 — Payment Info**
- bKash: xxxxxxxxxx | Nagad: xxxxxxxxxx | Bank: [Details if provided]

**Section 4 — Cars Under This Business**
- Summary: "3 Cars Registered" with status breakdown (2 pending, 1 approved)
- Link: "Review Cars →" → goes to 2C

**Action Bar (sticky at bottom of page)**
- "Approve Business" (green button) → modal: "Are you sure? This allows the owner to receive bookings." → Confirm → updates DB, sends SMS
- "Reject" (red button) → modal with mandatory text field: "Enter rejection reason" → Confirm → updates DB, sends SMS with reason
- (If already approved): "Suspend Business" | "Block Business" buttons (danger style)

---

### 2C — Car-Level Review Page

**Header:** Business name + "All Cars" + "Add Car" note

**Car List (per car, as cards):**

Each car card shows:
- Car photo (front)
- Model | Plate | Type | Seats | Color | Year
- Status badge: Pending / Approved / Rejected / Suspended
- "Review" button

**Car Review Panel (opens on click, full page or slide-in panel):**

- Car photos: 3 image slots (Front / Back / Interior) — click to enlarge
- Car details (read-only): model, plate, type, seats, color, year
- Documents section:
  - BRTA Paper: [Viewer] — "Mark Verified ✓" checkbox
  - Fitness Certificate: [Viewer] — Expiry Date: [date shown] — "Mark Verified ✓" checkbox
  - Tax Token: [Viewer] — Expiry Date: [date shown] — "Mark Verified ✓" checkbox
  - Insurance: [Viewer or "Not provided"]
- Driver Assigned: [Driver name + photo] or "No driver assigned" + "Assign Driver" button

**Action Bar:**
- "Approve This Car" → DB: `cars.status = 'active'` — does NOT affect other cars under same business
- "Reject This Car" → mandatory reason field → DB: `cars.status = 'rejected'`, reason stored
- "Suspend Car" (manual) → DB: `cars.status = 'suspended'`

---

### 2D — Driver Review

**Driver List Table:**
| Driver Name | Phone | License # | Assigned Car | Submitted | Status | Action |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

**Driver Detail View:**
- Name, Phone, Experience
- License front + back (image viewers)
- Driver photo
- Assigned car info
- Action buttons: "Approve" | "Suspend" | "Block"

---

## Panel 3 — Booking Panel

### 3A — Booking List

**Filters:**
- Status tabs: All | Pending | Confirmed | Ongoing | Completed | Cancelled
- Service type dropdown: All / Car Rental / Airport / Intercity / Tour / Event / Corporate
- Date range picker
- Area filter dropdown
- Search: booking ID or customer phone

**Table Columns (Desktop):**
| Booking ID | Customer | Service | Pickup Area | Date | Car Assigned | Status | Action |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

**Mobile Card:**
- Service badge + Status badge
- Customer name + date
- Pickup area
- "View" button

### 3B — Booking Detail View (clicking any booking)

**Page layout: 2 columns**

**Column 1 — Booking Info**
- Booking ID + Service Type + Status badge
- Customer info: name, phone
- ALL form fields the customer submitted (service type determines which fields show)
- Pickup date/time, location, car type preference, passenger count, special note
- Service-specific data rendered from `service_data JSONB`

**Column 2 — Assignment & Control**

**Car/Driver Assignment:**
- Current assignment: [Car model + plate] / [Driver name] or "Not assigned"
- "Assign Car & Driver" button → opens assignment modal:
  - System suggests cars matching pickup area + service type (auto-filtered)
  - Admin selects from dropdown of available, approved cars in that area
  - Admin selects driver from the business's driver pool
  - "Confirm Assignment" → updates DB, changes status to `confirmed`, sends SMS to customer

**Trip Control (state machine — buttons appear based on current status):**

| Current Status | Buttons Available |
|---|---|
| `pending` | Assign Car & Driver → leads to Confirmed |
| `confirmed` | "Mark Trip Started" (admin override) |
| `ongoing` | "Mark Trip Completed" (admin override) |
| `completed` | "Mark Payment Received" |
| Any | "Cancel Booking" (shows refund note) |

**Important:** The owner/driver triggers Start/End Trip from their dashboard. Admin override exists for disputes or manual correction.

### 3C — Payment on Booking (visible in booking detail)

**Payment Section:**
- Advance payment: ৳500 received via bKash | Transaction ID: xxx | [Paid ✓ badge] or [Pending badge]
- Final bill: [Input field if not yet entered] / [Amount shown if entered]
- Payment method: Cash / bKash / Nagad / Bank Transfer
- Amount received: ৳2,500
- Commission (10%): ৳250 (auto-calculated, shown in gold color, not editable)
- Net to owner: ৳2,250
- Payment status badge: Unpaid / Paid
- "Mark as Paid" button → updates `payment_status = 'paid'`
- Refund/Cancel note: if cancelled, show refund amount calculation

